{"type":"message","message":{"id":"gen-1775324587-6QVlSaO3nRRfK5XYBqv6","role":"assistant","created":1775324621,"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have the ESF balance data from the Treasury Bulletins. Let me extract the relevant data:\n\nFor June and September of 2000, 2001, 2002:\n- Total assets\n- Foreign exchange and securities (European euro + Japanese yen)\n\nFrom 2001 bulletin (page 112):\n- June 30, 2000: Total assets = 38,750,276; Foreign exchange = 6,634,663 + 8,877,769 = 15,512,432\n- Sept 30, 2000: Total assets = 37,094,883; Foreign exchange = 6,869,302 + 8,733,757 = 15,603,059\n\nFrom 2002 bulletin (page 115):\n- June 30, 2001: Total assets = 34,996,129; Foreign exchange = 6,817,884 + 7,595,657 = 14,413,541\n- Sept 30, 2001: Total assets = 36,353,790; Foreign exchange = 7,373,916 + 7,920,048 = 15,293,964\n\nFrom 2003 bulletin (page 113):\n- June 30, 2002: Total assets = 37,619,185; Foreign exchange = 8,198,962 + 7,879,571 = 16,078,533\n- Sept 30, 2002: Total assets = 37,591,058; Foreign exchange = 8,288,205 + 7,757,327 = 16,045,532\n\nNow I need to get CPI-U values to adjust to March 2003 dollars. I need to find the CPI-U values for:\n- June 2000\n- September 2000\n- June 2001\n- September 2001\n- June 2002\n- September 2002\n\n\n- March 2003\n\nI'll start by searching the Treasury Bulletins for the Consumer Price Index data.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_1ff6b5862e821c92","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"shell","arguments":{"command":"rg -i \"CPI\" /app/resources/treasury_bulletin_2003_03.txt | head -30"}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"developer"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
